# Every change to this repository is reviewed by the account that owns it.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES AND, MORE IMPORTANTLY, WHAT IT DOES NOT DO. On its own a
# CODEOWNERS file only requests a review; it cannot refuse a change. It becomes
# enforcement when the default branch carries a rule requiring review from code
# owners. Without that rule this file is a note about intent.
#
# The paths below are called out separately from the catch-all because they are
# the parts a change can break invisibly: a generated demo either works or looks
# wrong, whereas a change to how events are emitted, to a shared creative, or to
# the guard can be wrong on every future demo at once and still pass a glance.

*                               @Dengage-PreSales

# Event emission. One module owns every call to the Dengage SDK, and a demo's
# rows are only findable through the page view it sends.
/template/js/dengageEvents.js   @Dengage-PreSales

# Shared creatives. One file serves every live demo, so an edit here changes all
# of them at once, including demos already in front of a prospect.
/factory/creatives/             @Dengage-PreSales

# The guard and the checks. If these stop being strict, nothing else notices.
/factory/guard/                 @Dengage-PreSales
/factory/checks/                @Dengage-PreSales

# The factory itself: intake, generation and publication.
/.github/workflows/             @Dengage-PreSales
/factory/generate-demo.mjs      @Dengage-PreSales
/factory/scrape/                @Dengage-PreSales

# The operating rules and the specification.
/CLAUDE.md                      @Dengage-PreSales
/DEMO-FACTORY-HANDOFF.md        @Dengage-PreSales
